{
  "duration": 68.159,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.299,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.699,
      "end": 2.74,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.319,
      "end": 7.079,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, the speeds of two motorcycles are given in the ratio five is to six."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.539,
      "end": 10.96,
      "text": "The second motorcycle covers three hundred sixty kilometer in three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.34,
      "end": 13.739,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the speed of the first"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.139,
      "end": 16.639,
      "text": "motorcycle. Now, because the ratio is five is to six,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.039,
      "end": 21.939,
      "text": "we can take the two speeds as five x and six x. So first motorcycle speed is five times,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.299,
      "end": 30.84,
      "text": "second motorcycle speed is six times. Now, let us calculate the actual speed of the second motorcycle. We know that speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.179,
      "end": 34.52,
      "text": "So speed of the second motorcycle is three hundred sixty divided by three."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.88,
      "end": 39.499,
      "text": "That gives us one hundred twenty kilometer per hour. Now compare this with the ratio value."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.879,
      "end": 45.239,
      "text": "Second motorcycle speed is six x, and actual second motorcycle speed is one hundred twenty. So six"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.68,
      "end": 56.159,
      "text": "x is equal to one hundred twenty. After solving this, x is equal to twenty. Now we need the speed of the first motorcycle. First motorcycle speed is five x, and x equal to twenty."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.559,
      "end": 58.439,
      "text": "So five x is equal to five into twenty."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.84,
      "end": 61.019,
      "text": "That gives us one hundred kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.379,
      "end": 64.139,
      "text": "So the final answer will be one hundred kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.659,
      "end": 65.04,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.519,
      "end": 68.159,
      "text": "option B, one hundred kilometer per hour is correct."
    }
  ],
